#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186551292 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "021af7c8-298c-5829-b9fa-fc8322b9f50d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "X({X}^{T}\\,X)^{-1}{X}^{T}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550375} {:answer/id #uuid "28ecf387-c091-569b-870f-de70138cb197" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "X({X}^{T}\\,X)^{-1}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550467} {:answer/id #uuid "6ca78b37-8471-59f6-984c-04f09b456143" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "({X}^{T}\\,X)^{-1}{X}^{T}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550637} {:answer/id #uuid "a5d7a022-1c16-5e7b-ba63-b8d6ebd79ac5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(X{X}^{T})^{-1}X{X}^{T}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550803} {:answer/id #uuid "ffaf612d-85b8-52f9-bacb-05a3a72950b8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "({X}^{T}\\,X)^{-1}{X}^{T}\\,Xy" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551055}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "({X}^{T}\\,X)^{-1}{X}^{T}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550637} :answer-field/id #uuid "b5f5769d-1629-52ad-a8ed-38afe0f42079" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551176}] :question/id #uuid "789ea0d3-54ac-52af-9aa3-c806bd076e69" :question/math-academy-id "q-139599" :question/problem "| $x$ | **$0$** | **$2$** | **$4$** | **$6$** | **$8$** |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $y$ | $-1$ | $2$ | $1$ | $-1$ | $3$ |\n\nConsider the data above and the matrices below. Find an expression for the vector of coefficients of the curve $y={\\beta }_{0}+{\\beta }_{1}x+{\\beta }_{2}{x}^{2}+{\\beta }_{3}{x}^{3}$ that best fits the data. \n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & {0}^{2} & {0}^{3} \\\\ 1 & 2 & {2}^{2} & {2}^{3} \\\\ 1 & 4 & {4}^{2} & {4}^{3} \\\\ 1 & 6 & {6}^{2} & {6}^{3} \\\\ 1 & 8 & {8}^{2} & {8}^{3}\\end{aligned}],\\,\\beta =[\\begin{aligned}{\\beta }_{0} \\\\ {\\beta }_{1} \\\\ {\\beta }_{2} \\\\ {\\beta }_{3}\\end{aligned}],\\,y=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The coefficients of the curve \n\n$$\ny={\\beta }_{0}+{\\beta }_{1}x+{\\beta }_{2}{x}^{2}+{\\beta }_{3}{x}^{3}\n$$\n\nthat best fits the data can be found as the least-squares solution $\\hat{\\beta }$ to the system \n\n$$\nX\\beta =y,\n$$\n\nwhere $X$ is the design matrix, $\\beta $ is the parameter vector, and $y$ is the observation vector.\n\nPre-multiplying this equation by ${X}^{T},$ we obtain the corresponding normal equation\n\n$$\n{X}^{T}\\,X\\hat{\\beta }={X}^{T}y.\n$$\n\nSince the columns of $X$ are linearly independent, the matrix ${X}^{T}X$ is invertible and \n\n$$\n\\hat{\\beta }=({X}^{T}\\,X)^{-1}{X}^{T}y.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186551295 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "277522b5-e3dd-5b89-81f3-5cdba4469a16" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550464} {:answer/id #uuid "77d648dd-908d-5044-81c9-f4c8de288371" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.75" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550670} {:answer/id #uuid "98ceb55d-c397-5695-99ff-7995f7e2e05a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.95" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550755} {:answer/id #uuid "b6eebac0-9289-5154-9d7a-80de8f6fa66c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550867} {:answer/id #uuid "b7b44784-1307-5ab1-8d5a-2ec2e4bf1930" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550873}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550873} :answer-field/id #uuid "87636227-a251-5be3-befa-08c44f225fa6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551146}] :question/id #uuid "7d2bfda5-1f22-5eca-90c5-42502b97859c" :question/math-academy-id "q-135564" :question/problem "There are three supermarket chains in a particular city: chain $A,$ chain $B,$ and chain $C.$ A study has shown that, each month\n\n- from the customers that prefer chain $A,$ $5\\%$ change to chain $B$ and $15\\%$ change to chain $C,$\n\n- from the customers that prefer chain $B,$ $25\\%$ change to chain $A$ and $25\\%$ change to chain $C,$\n\n- from the customers that prefer chain $C,$ $15\\%$ change to chain $A$ and $35\\%$ change to chain $B.$\n\nThe stochastic matrix that describes this situation is given below. What is the value of $a+b+c?$\n\n$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}0.8 & a & 0.15 \\\\ b & 0.5 & 0.35 \\\\ 0.15 & 0.25 & c\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We are given the following situation for each month:\n\n- From the customers that prefer chain $A,$ $5\\%$ change to chain $B$ and $15\\%$ change to chain $C.$ This implies that $80\\%$ of them continue to prefer chain $A.$\n\n- From the customers that prefer chain $B,$ $25\\%$ change to chain $A$ and $25\\%$ change to chain $C.$ This implies that $50\\%$ of them continue to prefer chain $B.$\n\n- From the customers that prefer chain $C,$ $15\\%$ change to chain $A$ and $35\\%$ change to chain $B.$ This implies that $50\\%$ of them continue to prefer chain $C.$\n\nWriting this information in tabular form, we obtain the following:\n\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"10\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\">From:</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"80\"><b>Chain A</b></td>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"80\"><b>Chain B</b></td>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"80\"><b>Chain C</b></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" rowspan=\"3\">To:</td>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"80\"><b>Chain A</b></td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.8$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.25$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.15$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"80\"><b>Chain B</b></td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.05$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.5$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.35$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"80\"><b>Chain C</b></td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.15$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.25$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.5$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n\nWe can write the corresponding stochastic matrix as follows:\n\n$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}0.8 & 0.25 & 0.15 \\\\ 0.05 & 0.5 & 0.35 \\\\ 0.15 & 0.25 & 0.5\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFinally, we have\n\n$$\na+b+c=0.25+0.05+0.5=0.8.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186551305 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0b396ec8-53e0-5310-8fc0-d03edc40d6c0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550397} {:answer/id #uuid "7f86339a-7a6f-5135-9a8f-2e0733563d58" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 3 & 4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550689} {:answer/id #uuid "8201ae36-77d1-5268-b86b-d92cec98d7c8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 6\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550696} {:answer/id #uuid "b9dd4f54-d60c-5901-8ed3-cbf9885ed260" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 2 & 3 & 4 \\\\ -1 & -1 & -1 & -1 & -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550880} {:answer/id #uuid "dacfb9cc-6705-5dbe-9c5d-2ead3afed923" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 6 \\\\ 1 & 8 \\\\ 1 & 10\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550962}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550397} :answer-field/id #uuid "f3845349-5b5a-5657-a240-a68ca05150be" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551221}] :question/id #uuid "8779db6b-a3a9-5c0c-95e4-31a7bc1a4418" :question/math-academy-id "q-139572" :question/problem "| $x$ | **$0$** | **$1$** | **$2$** | **$3$** | **$4$** |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $y$ | $1$ | $3$ | $2$ | $4$ | $6$ |\n\nThe vector of coefficients  of the line $y={\\beta }_{0}+{\\beta }_{1}x$ that best fits the data above can be found using linear regression as \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}{\\beta }_{0} \\\\ {\\beta }_{1}\\end{aligned}]=({X}^{T}\\,X)^{-1}{X}^{T}y,\n$$\n\nwhere $X$ is the corresponding design matrix and $y$ is the observation vector. Which of the following is the design matrix $X$ in this context?" :question/worked-solution "| $x$ | **$0$** | **$1$** | **$2$** | **$3$** | **$4$** |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $y$ | $1$ | $3$ | $2$ | $4$ | $6$ |\n\nThe coefficients of the line that best fits the data can be found as the least-squares solution $\\hat{\\beta }$ to the system \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{X}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{aligned}]}}\\overset{\\beta }{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}{\\beta }_{0} \\\\ {\\beta }_{1}\\end{aligned}]}} & =\\overset{y}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]}},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $X$ is the design matrix, $\\beta $ is the parameter vector, and $y$ is the observation vector."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186551310 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3414a2fb-1c40-5baf-b160-d62aa452c159" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-2+4x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550495} {:answer/id #uuid "580265ce-7676-517c-8e36-74524881eba6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=2-4x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550583} {:answer/id #uuid "6f203b32-367e-5763-8e6c-d666dfea11ee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=4-2x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550646} {:answer/id #uuid "b301229a-92bc-5022-a48f-18260e3a02d2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=2+4x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550855} {:answer/id #uuid "e41db3bb-d1d9-5070-ae1b-2af09a13aaa7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=4+2x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550990}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=4-2x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550646} :answer-field/id #uuid "b80c480a-b5ef-5b14-b066-cb5d8f7268c9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551178}] :question/id #uuid "95655e19-4263-5e26-a218-4871ce1b1f2c" :question/math-academy-id "q-139645" :question/problem "| $x$ | **$-3$** | **$0$** | **$1$** | **$2$** |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $y$ | $9$ | $6$ | $3$ | $-2$ |\n\nFind the line of the form $y={\\beta }_{0}+{\\beta }_{1}x$ that best fits the data above.\n\n*Hint: You can use the fact that*\n\n$$\n({X}^{T}\\,X)^{-1}=\\frac{1}{56}[\\begin{aligned}14 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{aligned}],\\,{X}^{T}y=[\\begin{aligned}16 \\\\ -28\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\n*where $X$ is the corresponding design matrix and $y$ is the observation vector.*" :question/worked-solution "The coefficients of the line that best fits the data can be found as the least-squares solution $\\hat{\\beta }$ to the system  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{X}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]}}\\overset{\\beta }{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}{\\beta }_{0} \\\\ {\\beta }_{1}\\end{aligned}]}} & =\\overset{y}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]}},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $X$ is the design matrix, $\\beta $ is the parameter vector, and $y$ is the observation vector.\n\nPre-multiplying this equation by ${X}^{T},$ we obtain the corresponding normal equation\n\n$$\n{X}^{T}\\,X\\hat{\\beta }={X}^{T}y.\n$$\n\nSince the columns of $X$ are linearly independent, the matrix ${X}^{T}X$ is invertible and \n\n$$\n\\hat{\\beta }=({X}^{T}\\,X)^{-1}{X}^{T}y.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given values of $({X}^{T}X)^{-1}$ and ${X}^{T}y$ into the formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\hat{\\beta } & =({X}^{T}\\,X)^{-1}{X}^{T}\\,y \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{56}[\\begin{aligned}14 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}16 \\\\ -28\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, $y=4-2x.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186551325 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "903bfffc-e426-59e3-ab24-11a7979aa4ac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "300" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550734} {:answer/id #uuid "a380b557-2215-594c-843f-24dc64b7b436" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "320" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550792} {:answer/id #uuid "b0e2774b-270a-55ce-93a5-e9e33d94f09e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "380" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550850} {:answer/id #uuid "b1a5f251-9496-5266-9006-9a8c00b395c5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "420" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550852} {:answer/id #uuid "e100991f-d084-5436-83ef-32e93d923689" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "450" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550982}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "380" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550850} :answer-field/id #uuid "d3eedce2-2377-5540-8cff-1c60ab867920" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551201}] :question/id #uuid "af97554b-6ce7-555f-8ebb-05f560ef6317" :question/math-academy-id "q-135463" :question/problem "A certain store sells three types of instant soups: chicken, meat, and vegetable. The following table describes how the number of customers changes between the three types of instant soups each month:\n\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"10\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\">From:</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"60\"><b>Chicken</b></td>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"60\"><b>Meat</b></td>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"60\"><b>Vegetable</b></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" rowspan=\"3\">To:</td>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"60\"><b>Chicken</b></td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.4$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.2$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.3$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"60\"><b>Meat</b></td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.3$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.4$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.2$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"60\"><b>Vegetable</b></td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.3$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.4$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.5$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n\nFor example, $30\\%$ of chicken soup customers switch to vegetable each month, and $20\\%$ of vegetable customers switch to meat.\n\nCurrently, $400$ customers buy chicken soup, $400$ customers buy meat soup, and $200$ customers buy vegetable soup. How many customers will purchase vegetable instant soup in one month? You may assume that the total number of customers doesn't change." :question/worked-solution "From the table, we can build the corresponding stochastic matrix: \n\n$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}0.4 & 0.2 & 0.3 \\\\ 0.3 & 0.4 & 0.2 \\\\ 0.3 & 0.4 & 0.5\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe vector describing the number of customers for each type of instant soup is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}400 \\\\ 400 \\\\ 200\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nDividing the vector above by the total number of customers $(1\\,000),$ we get the stochastic vector of the initial state:\n\n$$\n{x}_{0}=\\frac{1}{1\\,000}[\\begin{aligned}400 \\\\ 400 \\\\ 200\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0.4 \\\\ 0.4 \\\\ 0.2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nTo find the state vector ${x}_{1}$ after one month, we apply one step of the Markov chain:\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}=P{x}_{0}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =P{x}_{0} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0.4 & 0.2 & 0.3 \\\\ 0.3 & 0.4 & 0.2 \\\\ 0.3 & 0.4 & 0.5\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0.4 \\\\ 0.4 \\\\ 0.2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0.3 \\\\ 0.32 \\\\ 0.38\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, after one month, $38\\%$ of customers will buy vegetable soup. Computing $38\\%$ of $1\\,000,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n1\\,000\\cdot 0.38=380.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $380$ customers will buy vegetable instant soup in one month."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186551332 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0296fe2c-3620-54f1-9ba1-56fc76e2a57d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & -6 \\\\ 1 & -4 \\\\ 1 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550378} {:answer/id #uuid "7835779c-d98b-5054-95c1-feb0292ef6ee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & -6 \\\\ 1 & -5 \\\\ 1 & -4 \\\\ 1 & -3 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550673} {:answer/id #uuid "962f0311-8a0a-531a-b2a4-eb199b394c72" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ -6 & -4 & -2 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550749} {:answer/id #uuid "a2030c00-81cb-582d-8ab1-8b808a0ea7d7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-6 & 1 \\\\ -4 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550786} {:answer/id #uuid "f3177ddd-2ea5-5752-a73b-5a4850d40c00" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-6 & -4 & -2 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 1 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551019}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & -6 \\\\ 1 & -4 \\\\ 1 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550378} :answer-field/id #uuid "9c2c5892-f74c-576d-86e2-c3d98f1ea70e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551159}] :question/id #uuid "c02b9ef4-844a-58b2-be01-9b59908adb2c" :question/math-academy-id "q-139574" :question/problem "| $x$ | **$-6$** | **$-4$** | **$-2$** | **$0$** | **$2$** |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $y$ | $1$ | $5$ | $8$ | $11$ | $15$ |\n\nThe vector of coefficients  of the line $y={\\beta }_{0}+{\\beta }_{1}x$ that best fits the data above can be found using linear regression as \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}{\\beta }_{0} \\\\ {\\beta }_{1}\\end{aligned}]=({X}^{T}\\,X)^{-1}{X}^{T}y,\n$$\n\nwhere $X$ is the corresponding design matrix and $y$ is the observation vector. Which of the following is the design matrix $X$ in this context?" :question/worked-solution "| $x$ | **$-6$** | **$-4$** | **$-2$** | **$0$** | **$2$** |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $y$ | $1$ | $5$ | $8$ | $11$ | $15$ |\n\nThe coefficients of the line that best fits the data can be found as the least-squares solution $\\hat{\\beta }$ to the system \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{X}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}1 & -6 \\\\ 1 & -4 \\\\ 1 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]}}\\overset{\\beta }{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}{\\beta }_{0} \\\\ {\\beta }_{1}\\end{aligned}]}} & =\\overset{y}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 8 \\\\ 11 \\\\ 15\\end{aligned}]}},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $X$ is the design matrix, $\\beta $ is the parameter vector, and $y$ is the observation vector."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186551337 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0334f116-416e-5d14-b3bf-b66d4f75de11" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$8.25$  points per game" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550380} {:answer/id #uuid "33db2298-5797-5cb1-af3d-bf806c19e083" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$7.75$  points per game" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550493} {:answer/id #uuid "bd226916-bde7-517b-871e-7e8629dd5812" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$8$  points per game" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550887} {:answer/id #uuid "d2b10de6-86fa-53ca-94d7-3e008b6bfb17" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$9$  points per game" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550935} {:answer/id #uuid "f5961ae6-fa3a-550a-9ffb-b71a8701df1f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$8.75$  points per game" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551025}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$8$  points per game" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550887} :answer-field/id #uuid "5784eef9-0ad2-5040-8dd4-135f8ec74797" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551117}] :question/id #uuid "d6dbf98c-84c4-5c67-a15a-4f405cbbd0b5" :question/math-academy-id "q-41401" :question/problem "The height (in feet) and the average number of points scored per game (APG) of four players on a basketball team are shown in the following table. \n\n| Height $(x)$ | **$6$** | **$6.5$** | **$6.5$** | **$7$** |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| APG $(y)$ | $5$ | $8$ | $10$ | $10$ |\n\nFind the line of the form $y={\\beta }_{0}+{\\beta }_{1}x$ that best fits the data above. According to the model, what will be the average number of points scored per game by a player whose height is $6.45\\,\\text{ft}?$\n\n*Hint: You can use the fact that*\n\n$$\n({X}^{T}\\,X)^{-1}=[\\begin{aligned}84.75 & -13 \\\\ -13 & 2\\end{aligned}],\\,{X}^{T}y=[\\begin{aligned}33 \\\\ 217\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\n*where $X$ is the corresponding design matrix and $y$ is the observation vector.*" :question/worked-solution "The coefficients of the line that best fits the data can be found as the least-squares solution $\\hat{\\beta }$ to the system \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{X}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 6 \\\\ 1 & 6.5 \\\\ 1 & 6.5 \\\\ 1 & 7\\end{aligned}]}}\\overset{\\beta }{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}{\\beta }_{0} \\\\ {\\beta }_{1}\\end{aligned}]}} & =\\overset{y}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 8 \\\\ 10 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}]}},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $X$ is the design matrix, $\\beta $ is the parameter vector, and $y$ is the observation vector.\n\nPre-multiplying this equation by ${X}^{T},$ we obtain the corresponding normal equation\n\n$$\n{X}^{T}\\,X\\hat{\\beta }={X}^{T}y.\n$$\n\nSince the columns of $X$ are linearly independent, the matrix ${X}^{T}X$ is invertible and \n\n$$\n\\hat{\\beta }=({X}^{T}\\,X)^{-1}{X}^{T}y.\n$$\n\n \n\nSubstituting the given values of $({X}^{T}X)^{-1}$ and ${X}^{T}y$ into the formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\hat{\\beta } & =({X}^{T}\\,X)^{-1}{X}^{T}\\,y \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}84.75 & -13 \\\\ -13 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}33 \\\\ 217\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-24.25 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have the line $y=-24.25+5x.$ \n\nFinally, to predict the average number of points scored per game by a player whose height is $6.45\\,\\text{ft},$  we substitute $x=6.45$ into the equation of the line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-24.25+5(6.45) \\\\  & =8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, according to the model,  the average number of points scored per game by a player whose height is $6.45\\,\\text{ft}$ will be $8$  points per game."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186551340 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "625975e6-7869-5a67-bc59-519fa2d8371d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550604} {:answer/id #uuid "65dd863d-70c0-5170-aa9a-00b0ab5e1a31" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}(-5)^{2} \\\\ (-25)^{2} \\\\ {5}^{2} \\\\ {20}^{2} \\\\ {35}^{2}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550618} {:answer/id #uuid "a348d2b4-ce93-5a99-a6ed-1906d407475a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}(-3)^{2} \\\\ (-1)^{2} \\\\ {1}^{2} \\\\ {3}^{2} \\\\ {5}^{2}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550791} {:answer/id #uuid "a61433c9-2b22-57c8-9478-14e323e7d6b6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ -25 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 20 \\\\ 35\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550804} {:answer/id #uuid "a6559ef5-d440-5051-9b33-5e541b8f53b5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550805}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ -25 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 20 \\\\ 35\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550804} :answer-field/id #uuid "b4aab56a-66ce-5d92-bf05-9bff500864c1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551175}] :question/id #uuid "d9bbc936-cdf8-5bb2-be25-3df4f1bc3232" :question/math-academy-id "q-139653" :question/problem "| $x$ | **$-3$** | **$-1$** | **$1$** | **$3$** | **$5$** |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $y$ | $-5$ | $-25$ | $5$ | $20$ | $35$ |\n\nThe vector of coefficients of the curve $y={\\beta }_{0}+{\\beta }_{1}x+{\\beta }_{2}{x}^{2}$ that best fits the data above can be found using polynomial regression as \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}{\\beta }_{0} \\\\ {\\beta }_{1} \\\\ {\\beta }_{2}\\end{aligned}]=({X}^{T}\\,X)^{-1}{X}^{T}y,\n$$\n\nwhere $X$ is the corresponding design matrix and $y$ is the observation vector. Which of the following is the observation vector $y$ in this context?" :question/worked-solution "| $x$ | **$-3$** | **$-1$** | **$1$** | **$3$** | **$5$** |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $y$ | $-5$ | $-25$ | $5$ | $20$ | $35$ |\n\nThe coefficients of the curve \n\n$$\ny={\\beta }_{0}+{\\beta }_{1}x+{\\beta }_{2}{x}^{2}\n$$\n\nthat best fits the data can be found as the least-squares solution $\\hat{\\beta }$ to the system \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{X}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & (-3)^{2} \\\\ 1 & -1 & (-1)^{2} \\\\ 1 & 1 & {1}^{2} \\\\ 1 & 3 & {3}^{2} \\\\ 1 & 5 & {5}^{2}\\end{aligned}]}}\\overset{\\beta }{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}{\\beta }_{0} \\\\ {\\beta }_{1} \\\\ {\\beta }_{2}\\end{aligned}]}} & =\\overset{y}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ -25 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 20 \\\\ 35\\end{aligned}]}},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $X$ is the design matrix, $\\beta $ is the parameter vector, and $y$ is the observation vector."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186551350 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0ec95535-d6a1-5444-a66f-12c14cc90adf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-3 & -2 & -1 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550408} {:answer/id #uuid "99538083-becb-52d4-9672-1fc2b387c331" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550756} {:answer/id #uuid "d3793b8d-2960-58c7-afcf-120f39097ca4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-7 & -4 & 2 & 5 & 10\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550938} {:answer/id #uuid "dfe4a5b1-a271-5ca0-b99e-5d25ada3dd88" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-7 \\\\ -4 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550980} {:answer/id #uuid "e2b5f77a-6357-5f9d-a83c-5e2d8467f25d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-7 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550987}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value