its the data above can be found using multiple linear regression as \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}{\\beta }_{1} \\\\ {\\beta }_{2}\\end{aligned}]=({X}^{T}\\,X)^{-1}{X}^{T}y,\n$$\n\nwhere $X$ is the corresponding design matrix and $y$ is the observation vector. Which of the following is the design matrix $X$ in this context?" :question/worked-solution "| ${x}_{1}$ | **$2$** | **$4$** | **$6$** | **$8$** | **$10$** |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${x}_{2}$ | **$10$** | **$7$** | **$5$** | **$3$** | **$2$** |\n| $y$ | $-4$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $8$ | $12$ |\n\nThe coefficients of the plane \n\n$$\ny={\\beta }_{1}{x}_{1}+{\\beta }_{2}{x}_{2}\n$$\n\nthat best fits the data can be found as the least-squares solution $\\hat{\\beta }$ to the system \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{X}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}2 & 10 \\\\ 4 & 7 \\\\ 6 & 5 \\\\ 8 & 3 \\\\ 10 & 2\\end{aligned}]}}\\overset{\\beta }{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}{\\beta }_{1} \\\\ {\\beta }_{2}\\end{aligned}]}} & =\\overset{y}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 8 \\\\ 12\\end{aligned}]}},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere $X$ is the design matrix, $\\beta $ is the parameter vector, and $y$ is the observation vector."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186557260 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "19864df4-2d2b-59b7-8b29-57ccd76568d5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-3.5-x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556484} {:answer/id #uuid "2ffa906f-87d9-5316-b4b0-5c81c75eda13" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=3.5-x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556532} {:answer/id #uuid "c73853c3-d2b8-5386-8f71-11b0dfc356a4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=1+3.5x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556909} {:answer/id #uuid "ca337b13-8de7-56cb-a6fd-dfe6db160da2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=1-3.5x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556914} {:answer/id #uuid "d6194152-573b-5c08-a9b7-e672113befaa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=3.5+x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556951}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=3.5+x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556951} :answer-field/id #uuid "32652aaf-8a9a-5672-9fc6-21a88c374b1a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557096}] :question/id #uuid "685118c5-b7fa-5fb3-b5f9-06f8a56c7a87" :question/math-academy-id "q-139647" :question/problem "| $x$ | **$-3$** | **$-1$** | **$0$** | **$4$** |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $y$ | $0$ | $2$ | $5$ | $7$ |\n\nFind the line of the form $y={\\beta }_{0}+{\\beta }_{1}x$ that best fits the data above.\n\n*Hint: You can use the fact that*\n\n$$\n({X}^{T}\\,X)^{-1}=\\frac{1}{104}[\\begin{aligned}26 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{aligned}],\\,{X}^{T}y=[\\begin{aligned}14 \\\\ 26\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\n*where $X$ is the corresponding design matrix and $y$ is the observation vector.*" :question/worked-solution "The coefficients of the line that best fits the data can be found as the least-squares solution $\\hat{\\beta }$ to the system  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{X}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 \\\\ 1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{aligned}]}}\\overset{\\beta }{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}{\\beta }_{0} \\\\ {\\beta }_{1}\\end{aligned}]}} & =\\overset{y}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]}},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $X$ is the design matrix, $\\beta $ is the parameter vector, and $y$ is the observation vector.\n\nPre-multiplying this equation by ${X}^{T},$ we obtain the corresponding normal equation\n\n$$\n{X}^{T}\\,X\\hat{\\beta }={X}^{T}y.\n$$\n\nSince the columns of $X$ are linearly independent, the matrix ${X}^{T}X$ is invertible and \n\n$$\n\\hat{\\beta }=({X}^{T}\\,X)^{-1}{X}^{T}y.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given values of $({X}^{T}X)^{-1}$ and ${X}^{T}y$ into the formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\hat{\\beta } & =({X}^{T}\\,X)^{-1}{X}^{T}\\,y \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{104}[\\begin{aligned}26 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}14 \\\\ 26\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3.5 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, $y=3.5+x.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186557275 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0878219e-c2fd-51d0-8c0f-8887e9b9bcc2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ -6 & -3 & 0 & 4 & 6\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556448} {:answer/id #uuid "5fda055d-c731-555a-bf72-502387bb59a3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & -6 \\\\ 1 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 6\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556646} {:answer/id #uuid "74dde18c-c7c1-59de-833d-07f07f975058" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-15 & -6 \\\\ -10 & -3 \\\\ -5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 \\\\ 5 & 6\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556695} {:answer/id #uuid "8987fbb9-4e36-5a31-a1b1-46618db9cc66" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & -15 \\\\ 1 & -10 \\\\ 1 & -5 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 5\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556757} {:answer/id #uuid "f2120fda-c38d-5064-839f-093917dee005" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ -15 & -10 & -5 & 0 & 5\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557027}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & -15 \\\\ 1 & -10 \\\\ 1 & -5 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 5\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556757} :answer-field/id #uuid "3086de9f-7992-5290-a78e-b92ab10911d8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557095}] :question/id #uuid "7fc30a95-4823-5308-bc3d-c38eeb6c9b5d" :question/math-academy-id "q-139576" :question/problem "| $x$ | **$-15$** | **$-10$** | **$-5$** | **$0$** | **$5$** |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $y$ | $-6$ | $-3$ | $0$ | $4$ | $6$ |\n\nThe vector of coefficients  of the line $y={\\beta }_{0}+{\\beta }_{1}x$ that best fits the data above can be found using linear regression as \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}{\\beta }_{0} \\\\ {\\beta }_{1}\\end{aligned}]=({X}^{T}\\,X)^{-1}{X}^{T}y,\n$$\n\nwhere $X$ is the corresponding design matrix and $y$ is the observation vector. Which of the following is the design matrix $X$ in this context?" :question/worked-solution "| $x$ | **$-15$** | **$-10$** | **$-5$** | **$0$** | **$5$** |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $y$ | $-6$ | $-3$ | $0$ | $4$ | $6$ |\n\nThe coefficients of the line that best fits the data can be found as the least-squares solution $\\hat{\\beta }$ to the system \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{X}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}1 & -15 \\\\ 1 & -10 \\\\ 1 & -5 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 5\\end{aligned}]}}\\overset{\\beta }{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}{\\beta }_{0} \\\\ {\\beta }_{1}\\end{aligned}]}} & =\\overset{y}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]}},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $X$ is the design matrix, $\\beta $ is the parameter vector, and $y$ is the observation vector."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186557294 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0ee8c8a2-5158-57a0-ad6b-eab622688ddb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 3 & 5 & 7\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556457} {:answer/id #uuid "1b31021f-f26a-5c88-9e24-49dab0b11f94" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 8 \\\\ 1 & 11 \\\\ 1 & 14 \\\\ 1 & 20\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556490} {:answer/id #uuid "593ac918-30c0-55f9-9a45-8bca67e90e57" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 7\\end{aligned}]" :d