. \n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & {0}^{2} & {0}^{3} \\\\ 1 & 1 & {1}^{2} & {1}^{3} \\\\ 1 & 2 & {2}^{2} & {2}^{3} \\\\ 1 & 3 & {3}^{2} & {3}^{3} \\\\ 1 & 4 & {4}^{2} & {4}^{3}\\end{aligned}],\\,\\beta =[\\begin{aligned}{\\beta }_{0} \\\\ {\\beta }_{1} \\\\ {\\beta }_{2} \\\\ {\\beta }_{3}\\end{aligned}],\\,y=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The coefficients of the curve \n\n$$\ny={\\beta }_{0}+{\\beta }_{1}x+{\\beta }_{2}{x}^{2}+{\\beta }_{3}{x}^{3}\n$$\n\nthat best fits the data can be found as the least-squares solution $\\hat{\\beta }$ to the system \n\n$$\nX\\beta =y,\n$$\n\nwhere $X$ is the design matrix, $\\beta $ is the parameter vector, and $y$ is the observation vector.\n\nPre-multiplying this equation by ${X}^{T},$ we obtain the corresponding normal equation\n\n$$\n{X}^{T}\\,X\\hat{\\beta }={X}^{T}y.\n$$\n\nSince the columns of $X$ are linearly independent, the matrix ${X}^{T}X$ is invertible and \n\n$$\n\\hat{\\beta }=({X}^{T}\\,X)^{-1}{X}^{T}y.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186558492 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7093db9c-29cd-58b2-bc04-0f2e75da08e3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & {1}^{2} \\\\ 1 & 2 & {2}^{2} \\\\ 1 & 3 & {3}^{2} \\\\ 1 & 4 & {4}^{2} \\\\ 1 & 5 & {5}^{2}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558088} {:answer/id #uuid "8b352bd0-126e-50a2-bef5-7ad0f9b65eb8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-20 \\\\ -10 \\\\ 40 \\\\ 20 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558141} {:answer/id #uuid "b9b70d6f-3a7e-54f3-b795-e1e558102083" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & -20 & (-20)^{2} \\\\ 1 & -10 & (-10)^{2} \\\\ 1 & 40 & {40}^{2} \\\\ 1 & 20 & {20}^{2} \\\\ 1 & 10 & {10}^{2}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558240} {:answer/id #uuid "d7fd9ca4-29c6-5fdc-a096-cd7801d7ab8d" :answer/type {:db/ident 